  "id": "ergo-antz",
  "title": "ergo antz",
  "subtitle": "A Found-Footage Audio Drama",
  "description": "ergo antz is a found-footage audio drama with foreboding, supernatural spinnings. Ambivalent forces torment an unwitting young woman. A flailing boyfriend struggles to navigate his partner's newfound obsessions and paranoia. A mind-tapping enterprise is hungry to exploit them all. Follow our troubled heroine, Christine, as she documents strange and disturbing experiences that have begun to plague her. While she defies classifying her experience as a psychotic break...the day might not be long when she wish it were. Written and created by sam sarkisian and emma arbor. Original music and sound design by sam sarkisian. Voiced by sam sarkisian, emma arbor, and real-life jesse. ergo antz is considered a fiction podcast with science fiction and horror podcast elements.",
